WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.240
I am at one of the tallest wind farms in Europe.

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:06.240
Look at that! Isn't that beautiful?

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:08.240
You can't tell right now, but basically,

00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:11.040
when the cloud goes over, that is so high

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:14.000
that it casts a shadow on the cloud as it's passing by.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.700
But the reason I' m here is because of something you might not know,

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:19.700
which is why,

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:23.220
when it's windy wind farms aren't always on and rotating.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:24.520
And there are a couple of reasons.

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:29.000
One, is that wind farms aren't built to take extremely high wind speeds-

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.160
above 50-55 mph it starts to get dangerous

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:35.440
and this beautiful thing could rip itself apart.

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:38.880
So, at high winds they slam the brakes on

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:39.880
and they stop them running,

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:42.880
because the amount of energy they would lose from doing that

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:45.460
is much less than the amount of energy you would constantly lose

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:47.620
if you had to build this thing

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:50.380
to withstand hurricane force winds.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:53.640
The other reason is that the national grid

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:56.300
can't cope with more than enough power

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:57.300
being dumped into it.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:59.440
There are no giant storage batteries,

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:02.600
that can hold the entire output of a power station.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:04.300
So, what happens is,

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:06.300
if the demand is low,

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:07.940
then they will just turn off the ones,

00:01:07.940 --> 00:01:09.520
that are easy to turn off, like this.

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:11.180
And when demand rises again,

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:13.780
they will turn on this and hydroelectric power plants,

00:01:13.780 --> 00:01:16.060
in order to deal with instant demand.

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:17.580
Nuclear, coal, gas-

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:19.320
all much harder to shut down,

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:21.240
all much harder to start up.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:24.440
And so, the national grid keeps us balanced at 50 Hertz--

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:27.820
50 cycles a second, 60 in America, 50 in Britain--

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:30.200
by monitoring the plants like this

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:32.200
and turning them on or off,

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:33.660
as needs be.

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:36.940
And that is something you might now have known.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:40.700
[Closed captions by MM.
